\newcommand{\BookConventions}{\begin{itemize}\item A leading \UserPrompt\ denotes a regular shell prompt; do not type it.\item A leading \RootPrompt\ can denote a root prompt; examples identify privileged operations explicitly.\item Text in a terminal box is literal; example output is illustrative and may differ on your system.\item Italic placeholders such as \Placeholder{filename} must be replaced with your own values.\item \KeyChord{Ctrl}{C} means press the two keys together.\end{itemize}}
